# Kuicksilver for Swift

The Swift package of [Kuicksilver](https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver), a QUIC, HTTP/3 and TLS 1.3 library.
This repository holds no source code. It is the binary distribution of Kuicksilver: `Package.swift` declares one binary
target, `Kuicksilver.xcframework.zip` of the matching
[GitHub release of kuicksilver/kuicksilver](https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver/releases), with its SHA-256. Each
tag here (`@VERSION@`, ...) is made by the release of that version and names the release's commit
(`@COMMIT@` for @VERSION@). Issues and pull requests go to the main repository.

```swift
dependencies: [
    .package(url: "https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver-swift", .upToNextMinor(from: "@VERSION@")),
],
targets: [
    .target(name: "App", dependencies: [.product(name: "Kuicksilver", package: "kuicksilver-swift")]),
]
```

iOS 15 or newer. Before 1.0 a minor version may break the API, hence `.upToNextMinor`. How to use it from Swift, the
privacy manifest the framework carries and what App Store submission needs:
[Kuicksilver on iOS](https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver/blob/v@VERSION@/docs/guide/ios.md).

## Verifying

SwiftPM refuses a zip whose SHA-256 is not the `checksum` in `Package.swift`. That the zip is the one the project
released is shown by the release, not by this repository:

```sh
curl -sLO https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver/releases/download/v@VERSION@/Kuicksilver.xcframework.zip
curl -sLO https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver/releases/download/v@VERSION@/Kuicksilver.xcframework.zip.asc
shasum -a 256 Kuicksilver.xcframework.zip     # the checksum in Package.swift
```

then check the `.asc` against the release key (fingerprint `22C1 F2E4 FCE9 4B28 EB2C 7DB0 492A BD95 C8D0 EC68`) and that the
zip is a subject of the release's build provenance, as
[Verifying a release](https://github.com/kuicksilver/kuicksilver/blob/v@VERSION@/docs/verifying.md) describes;
`tools/verify/verify-release.sh @VERSION@` in a clone of the main repository does all of it, including this
repository's `Package.swift`.

